BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fused Mezuzah
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTSTAMP:20261101T165532Z
UID:71059d8e0a03713f9746ac1d27f1@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Create a meaningful and beautiful piece of glass art in this h
 ands-on fused glass mezuzah class. Participants will design and build a de
 corative glass mezuzah using colorful sheet glass\, frit\, and stringers. 
 You’ll explore composition\, color layering\, and basic glass-fusing tec
 hniques while creating a one-of-a-kind piece that reflects your personal s
 tyle. Once completed\, your mezuzah will be fired in our kiln. No prior gl
 ass experience is necessary—this class is beginner-friendly and guided s
 tep by step by one of our instructors. Important Note This class is for ed
 ucational/craft purposes\, the resulting glass is a decorative holder\, no
 t a ritually certified vessel\, and participants should consult a Rabbi fo
 r religious validity/kosher status of the scroll (klaf) and final product
 \, as the shop's process isn't halachically supervised. ⏳ Finished piece
 s will be ready for pickup approximately 2 weeks after class due to kiln f
 iring schedules. Ages &amp\; Safety Adults\, and children ages 9+. Childre
 n ages 9&#8211\;12 must be supervised one-on-one by an adult or teen. No e
 xceptions as this is a safety issue. Whether you’re creating this piece 
 for yourself\, as a gift\, or as a meaningful artistic exploration\, this 
 class offers a thoughtful blend of tradition\, creativity\, and molten mag
 ic. What to Expect An introduction to fused glass safety\, materials\, and
  basic design techniques Design and assemble a decorative fused glass mezu
 zah front using sheet glass\, frit\, and stringers Your glass piece will b
 e kiln-fired after class and ready for pickup in approximately 2 weeks Par
 ticipants will be sent home with: A non-kosher scroll (klaf) A wooden mezu
 zah case Items are not assembled in class The finished glass mezuzah can b
 e adhered to the wooden case at home using E600 glue\, which is readily av
 ailable at most hardware stores\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.co
 m/event/fused-mezuzah/110083/
LOCATION:Blackstone River Glass Center\, 30 Meeting Street\, Cumberland\, 
 RI 02864
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/fused-mezuzah/110083/
END:VEVENT
